# Title: File Encryption/Decryption Via Gpg4win From Suspicious Locations
# ID: e1e0b7d7-e10b-4ee4-ac49-a4bda05d320d
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-11-30
# Tags: attack.execution
# Description: Detects usage of Gpg4win to encrypt/decrypt files located in potentially suspicious locations.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((cmdline:*-passphrase*) AND (((process_name:*\\gpg.exe OR process_name:*\\gpg2.exe)) OR (Product:"GNU Privacy Guard (GnuPG)") OR (Description:"GnuPG’s OpenPGP tool")) AND ((cmdline:*:\\PerfLogs\\* OR cmdline:*:\\Temp\\* OR cmdline:*:\\Users\\Public\\* OR cmdline:*:\\Windows\\Temp\\* OR cmdline:*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\* OR cmdline:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\*)))
